From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ilia Snezhkov <iasnezhkov@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 13:02:09 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] Honor mapped YUV planes and negotiate the encoder input
 layout

The RGBA Surface path allocated flexible YUV buffers but wrote them as
NV12. MindOne gralloc returns planar YV12 for the same allocation request.
The encoded Android Auto stream therefore had an empty upper chroma half
and displaced colors even though the luma geometry was intact.

Write semantic Y/U/V planes using their actual row and pixel strides,
and interleave chroma only for mapped semiplanar buffers. Validate mapped
bounds and supported 8-bit 4:2:0 layouts before conversion. Size temporary
chroma planes with rounded dimensions and check libyuv conversion results.

Negotiate the converted block's actual format before queuing it. Require
all plane strides and single-planar relative offsets to match the driver;
a matching format enum alone is not a compatible memory layout. Keep
conversion on the allocated pool when stride conversion is required.

The unmodified installed libraries reproduce the screenshot without a
head unit: a 1280x720 AVC Baseline Surface encode corrupts all 89 frames.
AHardwareBuffer lockPlanes reports Y/U/V offsets 0/1152000/921600 and
row strides 1280/640/640 with chroma pixel stride 1. This is YV12.
